{"file": "D:\\SpaceBook\\Books\\6th\\Math\\JPG\\109.jpg", "lines": [{"text": "Introduction", "conf": 0.893, "box": [[212, 119], [470, 126], [468, 170], [211, 163]]}, {"text": "between known and unknown quantity.", "conf": 0.954, "box": [[268, 359], [888, 340], [890, 387], [270, 406]]}, {"text": "6.1NumberPatterns", "conf": 0.917, "box": [[693, 452], [1145, 424], [1148, 468], [695, 496]]}, {"text": "Number patterns are sets of numbers that follow a pattern or", "conf": 0.921, "box": [[198, 566], [1164, 536], [1165, 589], [200, 619]]}, {"text": "PreviousKnowledge Check", "conf": 0.897, "box": [[1203, 566], [1606, 573], [1605, 614], [1203, 606]]}, {"text": "a rule.", "conf": 0.871, "box": [[203, 619], [311, 622], [310, 660], [202, 657]]}, {"text": "What ismeantbypattern", "conf": 0.888, "box": [[1208, 643], [1528, 643], [1528, 676], [1208, 676]]}, {"text": "The rule can be add or subtract a number each time or to", "conf": 0.905, "box": [[202, 672], [1106, 649], [1107, 698], [203, 721]]}, {"text": "ofnumbers,symbols,", "conf": 0.891, "box": [[1210, 684], [1478, 683], [1479, 717], [1210, 718]]}, {"text": "multiply or divide by a number each time. Each number in a", "conf": 0.914, "box": [[205, 727], [1145, 701], [1146, 751], [206, 777]]}, {"text": "colours etc.?", "conf": 0.908, "box": [[1207, 729], [1373, 724], [1374, 758], [1207, 763]]}, {"text": "sequence is called a term.", "conf": 0.896, "box": [[209, 787], [630, 778], [631, 814], [210, 823]]}, {"text": "Example 1: An author is writing a storybook. He wrote 2 pages on Monday, 5 pages on", "conf": 0.899, "box": [[204, 853], [1616, 819], [1617, 871], [205, 905]]}, {"text": "Tuesday, 8 pages on Wednesday and 11 pages on Thursday. If he keeps writing the pages in", "conf": 0.904, "box": [[207, 905], [1614, 874], [1615, 920], [208, 951]]}, {"text": "the same pattern, how many pages will he write on Friday, Saturday and Sunday?", "conf": 0.914, "box": [[209, 953], [1420, 927], [1421, 975], [210, 1001]]}, {"text": "Solution: Firstly, write the given pattern of pages written in a sequence:", "conf": 0.931, "box": [[218, 1023], [1354, 1003], [1354, 1050], [219, 1070]]}, {"text": "2, 5, 8, 11,", "conf": 0.876, "box": [[222, 1098], [393, 1098], [393, 1132], [222, 1132]]}, {"text": "Next, work out the difference in the terms. This pattern is going up by 3 each time, so we", "conf": 0.947, "box": [[219, 1148], [1622, 1121], [1623, 1167], [220, 1194]]}, {"text": "will add 3 to the last term to find the next term in the pattern.", "conf": 0.925, "box": [[224, 1202], [1196, 1190], [1196, 1227], [225, 1239]]}, {"text": "2, 5, 8, 11, 14, 17, 20", "conf": 0.863, "box": [[227, 1258], [568, 1251], [569, 1288], [228, 1295]]}, {"text": "So, the author will write 14, 17 and 20 pages on Friday, Saturday and Sunday respectively.", "conf": 0.917, "box": [[224, 1306], [1636, 1280], [1637, 1332], [225, 1358]]}, {"text": "Term to term rule", "conf": 0.795, "box": [[234, 1388], [589, 1379], [590, 1419], [235, 1428]]}, {"text": "The term-to-term rule of a pattern describes how to get next term in that specific pattern.", "conf": 0.93, "box": [[230, 1454], [1645, 1430], [1646, 1486], [231, 1510]]}, {"text": "Example 1:", "conf": 0.79, "box": [[237, 1514], [432, 1509], [433, 1550], [238, 1555]]}, {"text": "sequence.", "conf": 0.843, "box": [[241, 1627], [407, 1622], [408, 1657], [242, 1661]]}, {"text": "Solution : 11, 17, 23, 29,", "conf": 0.869, "box": [[243, 1674], [653, 1667], [654, 1703], [244, 1710]]}, {"text": "will add 6 to the last term to find the next term in the pattern.", "conf": 0.925, "box": [[241, 1766], [1227, 1770], [1227, 1826], [240, 1822]]}, {"text": "11, 17, 23, 29, 35, 41, 47", "conf": 0.853, "box": [[251, 1835], [650, 1826], [651, 1862], [252, 1871]]}, {"text": "all the terms in the pattern can be found.", "conf": 0.933, "box": [[258, 1988], [912, 1983], [912, 2026], [259, 2031]]}, {"text": "NOFRSE", "conf": 0.746, "box": [[372, 2091], [662, 2085], [663, 2121], [372, 2127]]}, {"text": "107", "conf": 0.749, "box": [[948, 2099], [1013, 2101], [1011, 2139], [947, 2137]]}]}